-- Fixture for `l4 export dmn`'s empty-model refusal (smucclaw/l4-ide#1104).
--
-- Both decisions evaluate under a rule date of their own (EVAL UNDER RULES
-- EFFECTIVE AT), and a DMN model has one rule-date input and no way to rebind
-- it, so the population filter (spec §2.5.6) leaves both out. The refusal
-- must name both under that reason, and must not offer --include-tests,
-- which does not bring a rebinding decision back.

IMPORT daydate

GIVETH A DATE
`the rule date in 2016` MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 9 2016) `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`

GIVETH A DATE
`the rule date in 2021` MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2021) `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`
